  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "5.1.3\n\nRecursive actions work. An action can now reference itself, directly or through other actions, as long as it reaches a wait before it recurses. 5.1 rejected every such pattern as a \"circular actionRef\".\n- When the recursive actionRef is the last thing left to run, the action restarts with the new params instead of nesting another copy of itself, so a pattern can recurse for as long as the game runs without using more memory or stack.\n- A cycle with no wait would loop forever in one frame, so it still fails to load: The action node \"loop\" has a circular actionRef with no wait before it\n- If a recursive action's waits come out as 0 at runtime (for example $rand*2), it runs once per frame instead of hanging.\n\nUpgrading from 5.0? 5.1.0 made pattern validation much stricter. See the full release notes before upgrading.\n\nFull release notes: https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
